vzvm: Unix-socket vsock forwards, and read-only shares.

A forward whose `listen` is an absolute path listens on a Unix socket. A
loopback TCP port is open to every local user; a socket in a 0700 directory
is not. A share takes `readOnly`, as a disk does. For pynix's Linux builder
(nixidae/nixidae#1138); to be offered to applicative-systems/vzvm.

